[Name] BinUtils
[Summary] Provides programs to assemble and manipulate binary and object files.
[License] GNU General Public License (GPL)
[Description] GNU BinUtils 2.43.1. The base GoboLinux 017.01 ISO ships
BinUtils 2.33.1, whose ld.bfd and ld.gold (hard-linked: the same binary
object) both predate SHT_RELR (.relr.dyn) support, added in BinUtils 2.38.
After the Glibc 2.44-2 upgrade, linking against libc.so.6 (whose dynamic
relocations live in a .relr.dyn section) fails with:
    ld.bfd: /lib/libc.so.6: unknown type [0x13] section `.relr.dyn'
    ld.bfd: cannot find /lib/libc.so.6
    collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status
This package provides a RELR-aware linker: ld.bfd is installed as the default
ld (--enable-ld=default); gold is deliberately disabled. Utilities include:
ld as nm objdump objcopy ar ranlib strip size addr2line.
[Homepage] https://www.gnu.org/software/binutils/
